    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15548" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-lūgĕo</span></b> , xi,
			2, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to mourn for</i> any 
			 one, <i>to be in mourning for</i>
			(rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virum (mulier),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					3, 2, 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib.
				11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patriam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 9, 20 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—With <i>cognate acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luctum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					7, 5, 4</span></i>
			.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid, cum eluxerunt, sumunt?</span>”
				<i>have completed their time of mourning</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 7, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
